  "description": "<p>Adelphi University is a prestigious university in Garden City, New York. A private institution dating back to its inception in Brooklyn in 1863; more than 8,100 students are currently enrolled at the University.</p><p>A powerfully connected doctoral research university offering excellent programs in various disciplines, Adelphi provides fantastic employment opportunities to its students with a hands-on learning approach.</p><h2>What is the Adelphi University acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The Adelphi University acceptance rate is 77.5%.</p> <p>The availability of medical care and counseling via the health and wellness center supports student health and wellbeing. The Center for Health Innovation, the Levermore Global Scholars Program and the Institute for Parenting are all excellent examples of the Universityâ€™s stellar research facilities.</p><p>There are two student centers with dining options, study spaces and more available for students to use at leisure.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Campus life is laden with opportunity at Adelphi University. There are more than 100 student organizations for students to get involved with and make new friends. Athletics is a big part of campus life as twenty-three NCAA Division II varsity teams play sports such as soccer, basketball, lacrosse and volleyball. A range of art exhibitions, concerts, plays, film screenings and more events are also hosted throughout the year for students with a different range of interests. Volunteer opportunities are surplus across campus as there is a big community feel and multicultural events to integrate students with other cultures.</p>",
